  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the main square of the medieval village of Grimaud, Le Café de France keeps up the spirit of a classic Provençal brasserie, with a shaded terrace ideal for watching village life while enjoying a simple dish.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is explicitly listed on the Grimaud tourist office's "dog-friendly restaurants" page (grimaud-provence.com/preparez/restaurants-dog-friendly-grimaud/), an official source that corroborates the confirmation already known. Open every day from 9am to 11pm, it's a handy option at any time of day. Average rating of 4.1/5 on Sluurpy (2,437 reviews): several recent reviews report a change of ownership with noticeably improved service since, worth bearing in mind if comparing with older, more mixed reviews.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: take advantage of being on the square to extend your walk through the medieval village's lanes before or after the meal.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Grimaud castle and the lanes of the medieval village are accessible on foot directly from the square.</p>
    </div>

